 obligations exceeded two billion dollars."}],"prose":{"overview":"Revenue reached $33.7 billion over the trailing year, while expenses grew 70% per year against 49% annual revenue growth. Committed money also grew 64% per year, showing that obligations expanded faster than sales.","debt":"Leases account for $378 million of committed money, while purchases account for $10.1 billion. Purchases therefore make up nearly all of the $10.5 billion total committed amount.","wall":"The next five years carry $9.5 billion of obligations against $362 million of revenue promised for that period. The due amount is 26.3x the revenue promised next five years. Backlog is $2.1 billion, equal to 0.1x one year of revenue.","flags_note":"The filings describe financing to related-party customers through trade credit and receivables from a corporate venture. Conditional revenue balances grew 7.6x while quarterly revenue grew 2.8x over the last 8 periods. The 10-K for the period ended 2024-06-30 was filed 240 days after period end, and the 10-Q for the period ended 2024-09-30 was filed 148 days after period end."}}